WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.560
The ontology operates entirely by reference.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.180
The metric you see in the

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.740
ontology simply acts as a pointer

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.540
back to that original source model.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.920
If the CFO changes the definition

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.140
of profit, your data engineers edit

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.500
the DAX expression in the Power

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.000
BI semantic model, just as they

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.940
always have. The ontology's role is

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.720
simply to provide a natural language

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.660
description and contextual metadata

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.060
so the AI agents understand what

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.420
that metric represents and when to

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.640
use it without ever altering or

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.759
copying the source math.
